      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Enforce pending-claim uniqueness atomically",
      "body": "With two simultaneous proposals for the same source member and target user, both transactions can observe no pending row and insert separate claims because the migration adds no matching unique or partial-unique constraint. This produces duplicate inbox entries and notifications and allows the copies to be completed independently; the deduplication must be enforced in PostgreSQL and its conflict handled.",
